{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS1yEninZyw4X2UPW6wz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've changed the generator, but the fix is untested: I didn't push anything, so nobody has checked it on the watch yet.\n\n**Cause.** `gen.py` built each heart-rate target as `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. In Intervals' workout format, `value` means a single target; a range is written as `start`/`end`. The watch notes point to this:\n- The watch showed its own zone bands, and they moved when you changed the watch's LTHR. That means it was receiving a zone number, not a fixed bpm range.\n- The zone it picked each time was the one containing the bpm of your *upper* bound (75%→129 is Z2, 93%→160 is Z4, and so on). The low end of your range wasn't getting through.\n- The API returning the event exactly as sent only shows it was stored, not that Intervals understood it.\n\n**Fix (`gen.py`).** The generator no longer builds `workout_doc` by hand. It now writes the workout as Intervals workout text in the event's `description`, which is what Intervals actually parses:\n```\n- Warm-up easy 10m 68-75% LTHR\n\n3x\n- Tempo 8m 88-93% LTHR\n- Float 2m 75-82% LTHR\n\n- Cool-down 5m 65-72% LTHR\n```\nIntervals then builds the workout itself and converts the percentages to bpm using LTHR 172. The watch should show 117–129, 151–160, 129–141 and 112–124, whatever LTHR it has detected. I also updated the README line describing what `gen.py` produces.\n\n**To confirm:**\n1. Run `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json && ./push.sh event.json`.\n2. Fetch the event again. Its steps should now have `start`/`end` and bpm values filled in by Intervals, rather than coming back exactly as sent.\n3. Sync to the watch and check that the tempo step reads 151–160.\n\nIf you'd rather keep sending `workout_doc` directly, the smallest change is `\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi` in `hr_target`. I went with the description text so Intervals' own parser builds the workout, instead of us guessing field names again.\n\nThe full reasoning, including why the earlier bpm attempts failed, is in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":325,"cache_read_input_tokens":29194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":325},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd6df4a-bf62-4c65-a30b-1adf25d54f77","uuid":"cda7cf75-e50b-4c4d-8fa6-51bf0306ab59","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:17:35.158Z","request_id":"req_011CgS1yEWrD3weRa9Q5dUHT"}
